  "worked_solution": "Note the following:\n\n- For a given joint PMF $f(x,y),$ we can think of each point where $f(x,y)\\ne 0$ as a point mass in the plane, where the \"probability mass\" at each point equals the probability associated with that point.\n\n- The joint CDF $F(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$ is the total \"probability mass\" that lies in the infinite rectangular region that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axis.\n\nGiven the supports of $X$ and $Y,$ the joint support $S$ is a subset of\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{3,6,9,12\\}\\times \\{2,4,6,8\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's plot the points in ${S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y},$ which contains the joint support, and sketch the region corresponding to the probability we wish to find.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14201862/assets/a782578ef55726c98ed23d89cf3de531ede60fe5db3fa9062c05507c5c2f60af.png)\n\nNotice that this region encompasses the same possible support points as the infinite rectangle with its top-right corner at $(12,4)$ and top-left corner at $(3,4),$ where the top and right boundaries are included, and the left boundary is excluded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14201862/assets/7ba99957a743b5cf283c2668e81b6c1aeb06730d47fc157aec90fe8bc880ced4.png)\n\nGeometrically, this region can be obtained by taking all points in the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(12,4)$ (the blue region below) and *subtracting* all points in the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(3,4)$ (the red region below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14201862/assets/3bd652b8d918e26cd330ad43555f039845d0b5405b70c96828bb2d652b7f872c.png)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6,Y\\le 5) & =\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(12,4)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 12,Y\\le 4)}}-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(3,4)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 3,Y\\le 4)}} \\\\  & =F(12,4)-F(3,4) \\\\  & =0.6-0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
